  "findings": "The annual chart confirms 60 EC in each year and the 30 EC elective block. The selection of Econometrics III, Mathematical Economics III and Financial Econometrics complies with both elective formulations. The two practical-entry rules and the 120 EC thesis threshold with relevant part-II course are explicit. UCR’s model-based economics and computational mathematics offer substantial response. Workbook evidence establishes genuine overlap in Markov decision processes and discounted investment appraisal. It also limits the overlap because VU extends into multistage stochastic optimization and traded-asset and portfolio theory. The energy option integrates climate, life cycles, conversion technologies, grid/storage constraints, public economics and a renewable-design report. It applies quantitative methods to energy choices without promising price forecasts. Current term/prerequisite constraints and 60 EC distinctness each way pass.",
